.TH STATE 1 "2026" "state" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
state \- system monitor: CPU, memory, disks, GPU and disk-usage treemap
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B state
.RB [ \-j | \-\-json ]
.br
.B state
.BR \-s | \-\-server
.RI [ HOST:PORT ]
.br
.B state dirstat
.BR \-s | \-\-scan
.RI [ PATH ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B state dirstat
.BR \-t | \-\-tree
.RI [ PATH ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B state dirstat
.BR \-l | \-\-list
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without arguments,
.B state
prints CPU (total and per core), memory, swap, disk free space and GPU usage.
.PP
.B state dirstat \-\-scan
measures which folders and files take up space under
.I PATH
and caches the result.
.B \-\-tree
shows a cached result for any path inside a scan, with the time it was scanned.
.PP
.B state \-s
serves a web UI (overview at /, disk-usage treemap at /dirstat) and a JSON API
on
.I HOST:PORT
(default 127.0.0.1:8084).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-depth " " \fIN\fR
tree levels to show (default 2, 0 = unlimited)
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-top " " \fIN\fR
biggest entries per directory (default 10, 0 = all)
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-one\-file\-system
do not descend into other filesystems while scanning
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
print JSON instead of text
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
no progress or summary output
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
print the version
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STATE_CACHE_DIR
where scans are cached; default
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/state/dirstat
or
.IR ~/.cache/state/dirstat .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/state.service
optional service for the web UI (not enabled by default:
.BR "systemctl enable \-\-now state" ).
It caches scans in
.IR /var/cache/state .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR du (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR free (1)
.PP
https://github.com/wildwind123/state
